Third-party code
----------------

The one-tap prompt pills (一键发送, client/quick-pills.ts) adapt the pill registration logic of
the quick-prompts plugin in kingsleydon/paseo-plugins
(https://github.com/kingsleydon/paseo-plugins, plugins/quick-prompts/client/pills.ts,
version 0.1.2): per agent, pills that keep their place are updated in place and the rest are
registered again from the first change. Sending is this plugin's own (its send ledger, which
never interrupts a turn without the user's OK). That code is used under the following license:

